            <ArticleTitle>Dielectric transitions and relaxations in Ca(ii)Co(iii)-based cyanometallate frameworks with a rare (6,6)-connected nia topology.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>45-48</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7dt03855k</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A series of cyanometallate frameworks A[CaCo(CN)6] (A = protonated guanidine, urea or thiourea guest) exhibit a rare (6,6)-connected nia topology with the Schläfli symbol of (412·63)(49·66) and thermally driven dielectric transitions and relaxations without evident structural phase transitions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
